Subject: [PATCH] lubot: chain: bud_aiGetCeilings okuyucusu geldi - kapi
 kirmizisi kapandi, sekim sozlesmesi burada

The red the queue had been carrying as `chain-surface-fixed` - registered
in `training/rpc-seti.json`, client nowhere in the production surface -
closes by writing the reader the registry's own note describes: a
read-only node query the operator's tooling answers, deliberately outside
`ALLOWED_METHODS` (the agent must not aim it at a node), so the client is
parse-only: no request builder, and the doc says so at the declaration
with the `WIRING:` marker the exemption rule provides - the node endpoint
that grows later has exactly one shape to satisfy, and this test pins it.

What the parser refuses is the whole design: a missing ceiling is refused,
not defaulted - reading "no value" as "no limit" is the one mistake a
ceiling reader must never make, so `0` is refused by name ("no-ceiling as
no-limit") rather than flowing through as truth - and an inverted effort
range is refused before a caller could honor one end by violating the
other. Zero, missing, inverted, errored: four refusals plus the happy
shape, one test; the `str_field`/`uint_field` idiom the file already speaks,
reused rather than paralleled.

`chain-surface-fixed` now reports 8/8 methods agreeing in both
directions (the gate's first green this queue has existed); all 25
cargo-free gates green; floor unchanged at 21/21 by design - the new
function is exempt at its declaration, not added to the baseline, because
an exemption that names its future caller is a record while a baseline
line is an excuse. README tables recounted from the applied tree (41 to 42
tools, 331 to 332 total), ratchet sentence extended. Not compiled: no
cargo (measured); serde_json is a live dependency of this crate already,
and every construct is the file's own vocabulary.
